@startuml blueprint
' Every Blueprint use case, the actors in each, and the System boundary.
' The text entries are the source; this diagram only shows how they fit together.
' View it with the PlantUML extension in VS Code, or render it with `plantuml -tsvg`.
' Smetana layout needs no Graphviz. SVGs are not committed.
!pragma layout smetana
left to right direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam monochrome true

actor Developer [[../actors/developer.md]]

rectangle Blueprint [[../system/blueprint.md]] {
  usecase "Run several Claude sessions" as Several [[../usecase/blueprint/run_several_claude_sessions.md]]
  usecase "Talk to Claude in a pane" as Talk [[../usecase/blueprint/talk_to_claude_in_a_pane.md]]
  usecase "Give Claude a use case as context" as GiveUseCase [[../usecase/blueprint/give_claude_a_use_case.md]]
  usecase "Know when Claude needs me" as Know [[../usecase/blueprint/know_when_claude_needs_me.md]]
  usecase "Run commands in a shell pane" as Shell [[../usecase/blueprint/run_commands_in_a_shell_pane.md]]
  usecase "Arrange my panes" as Arrange [[../usecase/blueprint/arrange_my_panes.md]]
  usecase "Review what Claude changed" as Review [[../usecase/blueprint/review_what_claude_changed.md]]
}

actor "Claude Code" as ClaudeCode
actor "Operating system" as OS
actor Git

Developer --> Several
Developer --> Talk
Developer --> GiveUseCase
Developer --> Know
Developer --> Shell
Developer --> Arrange
Developer --> Review

Several ..> Talk : <<include>>

Several -- ClaudeCode
Talk -- ClaudeCode
GiveUseCase -- ClaudeCode
Know -- ClaudeCode
Know -- OS
Shell -- OS
Review -- Git

' Hidden links fix the supporting actors' order, so no lines cross.
ClaudeCode -[hidden]- OS
OS -[hidden]- Git
@enduml
